AutoBrightness 0.1 (build 1) — macOS 27.0.1 (26A434), MacBook Air Mac17,4 (Apple M5), arm64
Built-in display id 1: "Liquid Retina Display", has ambient light sensor.
Decimal MB. Memory = TASK_VM_INFO phys_footprint and kernel lifetime peak. All app runs via LaunchServices (open -n -a).
Allocator flags in Info.plist LSEnvironment (process-local) — chosen by A/B, see research/Memory.md.

BUILD / CHECKS
./build.sh: -Wall -Wextra -Werror, ad-hoc signed.   codesign --verify --strict: valid on disk, satisfies Designated Requirement.
./test.sh (fake backend only; real setting untouched):
  PASS: unavailable symbols, unsupported Macs, read errors, ABI mismatch (unwritten byte, non-boolean byte, int-sized write),
        rejected writes, and unconfirmed writes.
  PASS: both states, press/keyboard/accessibility, busy guard, errors, unsupported state, direct menu-bar click (read-then-flip,
        failure opens panel, stale icon cannot override real state), panel freed on close and rebuilt, dismissal (Escape, outside
        click, second click), placement clamped to screen, rendering (transparent corners, translucent body, opaque with Reduce Transparency).

BACKEND EVIDENCE (research/Backend.md)
Disassembled signatures; same-process, cross-process and system_profiler ("Automatically Adjust Brightness: Yes/No") readback agreed
in both states; original value restored after each probe.

LIVE VERIFICATION  (--verify, final build; original = OFF)
  keyboard 0 (on) / accessibility 1 (off) / keyboard 2 (on) / accessibility 3 (off) / keyboard 4 (on) / accessibility 5 (off)
  menu bar click 6 (on) / menu bar click 7 (off) — each "verified by independent read"
  busy guard: PASS (second/third change while one in flight ignored; exactly one write)
  PASS: original setting restored (off) and read back independently.
  Earlier build, original = ON: same steps, all verified, restored (on).
  Final independent read after the run: Automatic brightness: off; system_profiler: Automatically Adjust Brightness: No.
  Note: the setting was found "off" before this run although it was "on" at the start of the task; it was not changed by the
  verification (which restores whatever it finds). Cause unknown: a copy of the app with the new click-to-toggle icon was running at the time.

ADDED: LOGIN ITEM, HOVER LABEL (final build)
  ./install.sh -> /Applications/AutoBrightness.app registered through SMAppService on first run; `sfltool dumpbtm`:
    Identifier 2.local.amogh.AutoBrightness, URL /Applications/AutoBrightness.app, Disposition [enabled, allowed, notified].
    Preference LoginItemRequested=1 (never re-registered, so switching it off in Login Items is respected). Not verified by an actual logout/login.
  Hover label: unit-checked (lines per state, one child at a time, appears only after 0.5 s, cancelled by exit/click/panel open, glass vs opaque card,
  clamping, Apple headline text style); live: `--verify` starts a real child, it stays up, and hideHover stops it (no stray process);
  rendered under the menu bar on the real screen as Liquid Glass with SF text (screenshot inspected). A physical pointer hover was not performed.

MEMORY (normal LaunchServices launch; first block measured before the hover label/login code was added)
  Plain launch, 6 s then 20 s idle, panel never opened:  footprint 7.849 MB, lifetime peak 8.144 MB
  --verify (idle before open / after interaction / lifetime peak):
     8.766 / 9.209 / 10.175 MB   (earlier runs of the same build line: 8.29–8.80 / 9.2 / 10.126–10.241)
  --profile (read-only; open + five reopens): idle 8.029, panel open 9.176 MB
  RESULT: 8.00 MB target FAILS (post-interaction lifetime peak 10.175 MB; plain-launch peak 8.144 MB).
  Cause: empty AppKit app + one NSStatusItem = 8.078 MB footprint / 8.422 MB peak with the same allocator flags (research/Memory.md).

IDLE CPU (20 s, after the panel closed; research/cpu-measure.c)
  pid=45888 (held after --profile): CPU=0.00299% CPU_time=0.598 ms idle_wakeups=1 interrupt_wakeups=3; activity only at 1 s, 2 s (panel teardown) and 18 s; footprint 9.97 MB, lifetime peak 11.371 MB (profile-mode run).
  Plain launch: CPU=0.00344% CPU_time=0.688 ms idle_wakeups=1 interrupt_wakeups=2; footprint 7.849 MB, peak 8.144 MB.
  No periodic wakeups.

NOT VERIFIED
  Physical VoiceOver run (accessibility roles/actions checked programmatically only); physical right-click/Control-click and
  Reduce Transparency toggled in System Settings (the override path and pixel output were tested); other Macs / macOS versions;
  an external-display-only Mac; kill -9 during --verify cannot restore.

FINAL BUILD AFTER HOVER/LOGIN CHANGES
  --verify (original = on): all steps verified, busy guard PASS, original restored and read back (on).
     idle 9.094 / after use 9.438 / lifetime peak 10.634 MB — 8.00 MB target FAILS.
  Installed plain launches, 6 s then 20 s idle: footprint 8.18–8.39 MB, lifetime peak 8.46–8.62 MB (some runs after a fresh install or with system activity
  showed 9.8 MB / up to 11.2 MB). CPU 0.0025–0.0034% (0.5–0.7 ms per 20 s); one run during system activity 0.30% (60 ms).
